                        "sense_id": "a5b779a4-106c-372e-a24d-32d8cb58cd2d",
                        "entry_id": "2d391929-5528-3a97-934e-6c8e67f3a1a9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The (possible) act of Finland leaving the European Union."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b3ca8b5-3af9-49cd-8b2a-3c23c47f864e",
                                "sense_id": "a5b779a4-106c-372e-a24d-32d8cb58cd2d",
                                "text": "In a statement on his official website, Vayrynen suggests that a Greek exit from the Eurozone would be an opportunity for Finland to 'Fixit' and potentially leave the EU common currency."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ad901d5-44c1-457a-8954-ab45c80b877e",
                                "sense_id": "a5b779a4-106c-372e-a24d-32d8cb58cd2d",
                                "text": "We've heard of a \"Grexit\" and \"Brexit\" to refer respectively to the threat of Greece and Britain leaving the euro zone and European Union. But now there's a \"Fixit\" – a Finnish exit of the single currency."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ea3ac21-8ecd-4926-b4fa-bb151d07fb5e",
                                "sense_id": "a5b779a4-106c-372e-a24d-32d8cb58cd2d",
                                "text": "Terho declined to say whether the Finns party would propose a \"Fixit\"-vote after Britons opted last week for \"Brexit\", but said it should be one of the main issues of the 2019 elections. \"If the people back it, then we should have a vote if we'll stay or leave.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
